# Microeconomics in the &quot;Framework:&quot; A Reconsideration.

**Authors:** Buckles, Stephen.

## Abstract
Reviews and critiques Strober's paper (see SO516707) on the scope of microeconomics instruction in United States schools. States that much of what is recommended by Strober would benefit economics instruction in both elementary and secondary schools; specifically endorsing increased emphasis on the role of values, efficiency, and equity within the Joint Council's &quot;Framework.&quot; (JDH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ356147

